& [Delineation_A_LanguagePurpose] is plain articulated semantic programming
  + SOP expresses intended meanings, identities, relations, conditions, contracts, operations, programs, and proof obligations in inspectable form
  + multi-target compilation projects one articulated meaning into exact, neural, hybrid, attention, data, tool, workflow, hardware, or interface artifacts
  + compilation does not make all SOP documents programs
  + source meaning remains distinct from compiled representation and runtime event

& [Delineation_B_ExecutionMeaning] separates five senses of execute
  + exact_evaluation applies deterministic SemanticIR semantics
  + neural_proposal invokes or materializes a learned target whose output remains provider-dependent
  + hybrid_evaluation admits or rejects neural proposals through exact contracts
  + tool_or_effect_commit invokes an external capability only after separate runtime admission
  + semantic_articulation describes executable form without executing it
  - never: substitute one sense for another without a typed transition

& [Delineation_C_NeuralPrinter] is bounded generation
  + compiler may emit a neural blueprint, initialization constraints, reviewed corpus contract, training plan, evaluation plan, or provider package
  + an LLM may propose graph topology, weights, examples, routes, or code as untrusted candidate material
  + generated tensors or artifacts require deterministic construction records where claimed, held-out evaluation, correspondence, and target admission
  + model fluency or source proximity does not prove semantic equivalence

& [Delineation_D_SemanticCenter] is exact-first
  + one canonical source-mapped SemanticIR carries identities, contracts, state, transitions, effects, uncertainty, and proof obligations
  + targets consume the same root through explicit capability profiles
  + exact meaning owns commitment, authority, constraints, faults, rollback, and termination
  + approximate targets declare every loss, nondeterminism, and provider dependency

& [Delineation_E_Compatibility] preserves the corpus
  + source, definition, data, contract, policy, profile, test, proof, narrative, manifest, program, and mixed documents remain distinct
  + unclassified historical SOP defaults to preserved and non-executable
  + only explicit program regions become executable candidates
  + prior signatures retain only their stated scope

& [Delineation_F_SelfDescription] is reflective but bootstrapped
  + SOP may describe its own profiles, grammar, semantics, passes, modules, targets, tests, and runtime contracts
  + self-description does not eliminate the need for one independently trusted parser, validator, serializer, signature policy, and fixture
  + a compiler cannot validate its own correctness only through artifacts produced by itself

& [Delineation_G_CurrentAuthority] is specification-only
  + purpose formation may define stable semantic roles and future interfaces
  + no parser, compiler, model, runtime, effect broker, database, service, CLI, FPGA, or provider is activated by this artifact
  + the first fixture remains a later separately claimed implementation slice

& [SMTC_001_LanguageIdentity] is atomic
  + define SOP as an inspectable semantic programming language with multi-target compilation
  + retain plain articulated meaning as source identity
  = verify: canonical purpose and language boundary
  - reject: AI-only identity or prose-only identity

& [SMTC_002_ArtifactRoles] is atomic
  + classify every compiling artifact by document and region role
  + keep non-program roles non-executable
  = verify: role matrix and historical default
  - reject: syntax-as-execution or signature-as-program

& [SMTC_003_ProgramAdmission] is atomic
  + admit only explicit SemanticProgram regions under complete SemanticContract
  + require source, resolution, static, lowering, proof, trust, and runtime gates
  = verify: ten-gate admission path
  - reject: implicit execution extent

& [SMTC_004_CanonicalIR] is atomic
  + preserve one canonical SemanticIR across accepted surface forms and targets
  + bind every node to source and role correspondence
  = verify: equal-root fixture
  - reject: backend-specific source meaning

& [SMTC_005_ExactTarget] is atomic
  + SOP-X represents deterministic exact execution fabric
  + unsupported exact behavior fails closed
  = verify: deterministic trace and result
  - reject: hidden approximation

& [SMTC_006_ExactAuthority] is atomic
  + exact semantics own commitment, authority, hard constraints, faults, rollback, and termination
  + runtime grant remains separate from compiler request
  = verify: authority and effect traces
  - reject: compiler output as runtime grant

& [SMTC_007_NeuralTarget] is atomic
  + SOP-N compiles fabric-bound neural proposal or generation artifacts
  + outputs remain advisory unless a narrower deterministic property is separately proved
  = verify: proposal typing and provider record
  - reject: neural answer as source fact or permission

& [SMTC_008_HybridTarget] is atomic
  + SOP-H surrounds learned proposals with exact admission, challenge, fallback, and refusal
  + exact behavior remains available when the learned path is unavailable
  = verify: accepted and rejected proposal cases
  - reject: learned target bypass of exact gates

& [SMTC_009_DerivedTargets] is atomic
  + SOP-A, SOP-D, SOP-T, SOP-W, SOP-F, and SOP-I are derived projections
  + each declares capability and loss boundaries
  = verify: target profile table
  - reject: new target without signed need and interface

& [SMTC_010_PackageLineage] is atomic
  + bind source, dependencies, compiler, SemanticIR, targets, proofs, runtime, provider, and results
  + preserve one PackageFamily identity across projections
  = verify: correspondence and manifest graph
  - reject: orphan artifact or mutable locator authority

& [SMTC_011_InstructionFamilies] is atomic
  + support DECLARE, SCOPE, RELATE, ATTEND, INFER, CONSTRAIN, TRANSFORM, CONTROL, EFFECT, and EMIT families
  + type every operation and result
  = verify: SemanticIR constructors and fixture coverage
  - reject: undeclared effect or control behavior

& [SMTC_012_StageSeparation] is atomic
  + distinguish describe, declare, compile, propose, evaluate, validate, authorize, commit, and observe
  + represent each as typed state or authority transition
  = verify: transition table
  - reject: proposal or description as commitment

& [SMTC_013_ContractCompleteness] is atomic
  + bind purpose, inputs, preconditions, assumptions, invariants, permissions, obligations, prohibitions, outputs, effects, faults, and termination
  + block incomplete entry points
  = verify: contract pass and missing-field negatives

& [SMTC_014_AttentionAndInference] is atomic
  + compile attention, inference, control, and effect primitives as typed behavior
  + preserve admitted focus, context, regimes, judgments, and uncertainty
  = verify: source-mapped attention and inference trace
  - reject: hidden prompt state as semantic authority

& [SMTC_015_EffectSafety] is atomic
  + distinguish pure, attention, epistemic, memory, database, file, Git, tool, provider, user-authorization, and external effects
  + keep propose, authorize, commit, and observe distinct
  = verify: effect rows, capabilities, and negative write case

& [SMTC_016_FacultyCompilation] is atomic
  + compile faculties as typed libraries and governed cycles over base primitives
  + retain Observer, Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Weaver, and Planner accountability
  = verify: faculty module and return records
  - reject: faculty names as magical primitives or decorative roles

& [SMTC_017_ReflectionAndReplay] is atomic
  + retain source, before-state, transition, result, proof, residual, and reentry lineage
  + support inspection without permitting inspection to mutate authority
  = verify: replay record and immutable source mapping

& [SMTC_018_LanguageCompletenessContract] is atomic
  + define grammar profile boundary, static semantics, kinds, types, relations, effects, modules, diagnostics, standard-library boundary, and optimizer laws
  + defer exact physical grammar and library membership to versioned profiles
  = verify: WS-CTPR-003 worker proof
  - reject: guessed physical design as core semantics

& [SMTC_019_CompilerAndRuntimeInterfaces] is atomic
  + define common TargetABI and RuntimeABI requests and responses
  + require target refusal on unsupported features or prohibited loss
  = verify: ABI field and refusal tables

& [SMTC_020_ConformanceAndCompatibility] is atomic
  + define cross-surface, cross-target, and independent-implementation fixtures
  + preserve explicit source, semantic, module, target, package, and migration compatibility
  = verify: positive and negative conformance suite contract

& [SMTC_021_NeuralGenerationBoundary] is atomic
  + separate blueprint, initialization, corpus, training, evaluation, admission, and packaging stages
  + preserve provider and stochastic dependencies
  = verify: neural target lifecycle
  - reject: prompt response as trained model proof

& [SMTC_022_ExactFallback] is atomic
  + preserve valid exact behavior when learned targets are absent, stale, uncertain, rejected, failed, or disabled
  + report degraded capability explicitly
  = verify: neural-abstention and unavailable-provider fixtures

& [SMTC_023_LLMCompilerRole] is atomic
  + an LLM may scan, propose, normalize, cross-reference, and form candidate compiler artifacts
  + deterministic tools validate identities, hashes, schemas, constraints, and correspondence
  = verify: proposal-to-admission trace
  - reject: model self-certification

& [SMTC_024_NeuralWeightClaim] is atomic
  + learned weights are approximate routing or generative state rather than authoritative SOP storage
  + authoritative terms resolve to inspectable source identities and digests
  = verify: retrieval proof and loss declaration

& [SMTC_025_HardwareProjection] is atomic
  + SOP-F may target an interpreter layer or native hardware fabric under separate profile
  + require resource, timing, correspondence, and equivalence proof
  = verify: hardware profile contract only
  - reject: current FPGA implementation authority

& [SMTC_026_FirstProof] is atomic
  + implement one tiny exact, neural-blueprint, and hybrid program only after separate implementation release
  + include instruction-shaped data and undeclared-effect negatives
  = verify: later deterministic fixture proof

& [SMTC_027_Measurement] is atomic
  + measure semantic preservation, execution, correspondence, proof completeness, fallback, conformance, and work cost
  + record unsupported or negative results
  = verify: metric schema and proof bundle

& [SMTC_028_VisibleFailure] is atomic
  + fail visibly on unsupported target features, ambiguity, authority gaps, prohibited approximation, or semantic loss
  + preserve actionable diagnostics
  = verify: diagnostic expectations

& [SMTC_029_TargetGrowthGate] is atomic
  + add a target only for signed requirements and measured benefit
  + require target profile, ABI conformance, proof policy, maintenance owner, and removal path
  = verify: target registration decision

& [SMTC_030_BootstrapAndMigration] is atomic
  + retain one independently trusted bootstrap and explicit migration records
  + preserve original source generations, interpretations, losses, obligations, rollback, and supersession
  = verify: bootstrap and migration contracts

& [RoleSet] is closed for purpose formation
  + [source_author] supplies preserved intention without self-signing derived authority
  + [SJS_processor] delineates, refines, tests constraints, justifies, registers, and signs bounded meaning
  + [language_profile_author] selects exact surface grammar and standard modules under later source
  + [compiler_implementation] parses and validates under separately released implementation authority
  + [target_backend] projects only declared target capabilities
  + [runtime] admits and evaluates only trusted packages and granted effects
  + [neural_provider] returns typed candidate material without source authority
  + [independent_verifier] checks expected meaning without reusing the implementation under test

& [StateModel] is governance monotonic
  + raw_source_preserved
  + assessed
  + delineated_exploded
  + semantically_refined
  + data_designed
  + constraint_checked
  + pruned_and_growth_seeded
  + seven_fold_phase_locked
  + justified_and_planned
  + registered
  + canonical_purpose_signed
  - no state includes implemented, compiled, packaged, admitted, executed, trained, deployed, synthesized, or effect_committed

& [FailureTable] is explicit
  + [F01] source overwritten or digest drift
  + [F02] all SOP reclassified as program
  + [F03] parser success promoted to execution
  + [F04] multiple incompatible semantic centers
  + [F05] backend hides loss or provider dependence
  + [F06] neural output promoted to fact or authority
  + [F07] imported module widens authority
  + [F08] effect proposal becomes commitment
  + [F09] optimizer erases provenance, faults, or effects
  + [F10] unsupported target receives guessed lowering
  + [F11] compiler validates itself without independent fixture
  + [F12] physical implementation claimed by purpose signature
  + [F13] prior signature scope silently expands
  + [F14] exact fallback depends on neural availability
  + [F15] target proliferation lacks signed benefit

& [AcceptanceTable] is exact for the purpose signature
  + [AC01] source and derived roles remain separate and content-bound
  + [AC02] every SMTC requirement maps to canonical clauses and proof route
  + [AC03] role-first static semantics and one SemanticIR are explicit
  + [AC04] target and runtime interfaces fail closed
  + [AC05] neural and hybrid targets remain subordinate to exact authority
  + [AC06] conformance and compatibility obligations are independently testable
  + [AC07] implementation, runtime, provider, hardware, and effect authority remain absent
  + [AC08] first implementation fixture is described but not released

& [ExhaustionEntry] is open
  + semantic refinement, data design, constraint ledger, pruning and growth, seven-fold exhaustion, justification, plan, registry, matrix, canonical specification, and phase lock remain separate artifacts
  + [current_authority] is none
